CommitDate: Wed Sep 30 23:58:04 2026 -0500

    feat: extend priority vocabulary to P0..P5 (BT-070)
    
    PriorityVocabulary gains P4/P5; NormalizePriority maps bare 4/5 and
    case/whitespace variants onto them; the write-time gate (create, update,
    import) accepts P0..P5 and its error texts name the new set; validate's
    BT-048 warning text reads {P0,P1,P2,P3,P4,P5}; titlePriorityToken matches
    single digits 0-5, so [P4]/[P5] title tokens are drift-checked again;
    update's --priority help text says P0-P5.
    
    Tests: create/update accept P4/P5 (+ bare 4/5, case variants); NormalizePriority
    table covers P0..P5 with junk pass-through; validate stays silent on P4/P5
    rows and warns naming the new set; token table gains [P4]/[P5] rows;
    BT-060's P4 row flips from silent to drift-warning (P4 is in-vocabulary);
    render pins P0..P5 ordering (P4/P5 after P3, lexical byte order — no rank
    table exists in the render path). Junk examples moved P4->P9 across tests.
    
    RED-proven: reverting the vocabulary map, the 4/5 normalize cases, the
    regex digit class, or the warning set-text each turns the new tests red;
    restored byte-identical after each probe.
    
    Addresses BT-070.
